      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(reply): suppress stranded retry after source message send",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw `message_tool_only` turns can successfully send the visible source-chat reply through `message(action=send)` and still be treated as undelivered by stranded-reply recovery. That false negative triggers the fallback: `I generated a reply but could not deliver it to this chat. Please try again.`\n\nThis PR makes source-route message-tool sends count as source-reply delivery evidence in both direct reply-agent runs and queued followup retries, while preserving stranded-retry behavior when the message tool sends only to a non-source target.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Updated direct reply-agent delivery checks to treat visible message-tool sends as delivered only when they match the source route/dedupe criteria.\n- Updated followup stranded-retry delivery checks with the same source-route matching, so successful source replies suppress retry diagnostics.\n- Preserved retry diagnostics for sends to non-source targets.\n- Targeted tests passed: `node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner.misc.runreplyagent.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/followup-runner.test.ts` (`216` tests).\n- Syntax checks passed: `node --check src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner.ts` and `node --check src/auto-reply/reply/followup-runner.ts`.\n- Whitespace check passed: `git diff --check`.\n\nNote: local `pnpm tsgo:core:test` was started in the fresh worktree but produced no output for several minutes, so it was stopped rather than left hanging; CI should run the full typecheck.\n",
        "branch": "fix/stranded-retry-message-tool-delivery",
